      {
        "id": "stage-1-topic-16-section-17",
        "title": "Production Hands-on Lab — Advanced Design Considerations",
        "content": "TOPIC: Production Hands-on Lab\nSECTION: Production Hands-on Lab — Advanced Design Considerations\n\nADVANCED TECHNICAL DESIGN:\nAdvanced design requires understanding the internal architecture, runtime behaviour, resource requirements and failure boundaries of Production Hands-on Lab. Evaluate how the design behaves under concurrent workloads, dependency failures, configuration changes and increasing production traffic.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION:\nSeparate responsibilities into cohesive components. Define explicit contracts, validate configuration and inputs, preserve error causes and avoid hidden shared state. Select implementation strategies based on measurable requirements rather than assumptions.\n\nTESTING:\nCreate focused unit tests and integration tests for normal execution, invalid input, boundary conditions, concurrency where applicable and dependency failures. Verify expected behaviour using repeatable Maven test commands.\n\nPERFORMANCE:\nMeasure CPU consumption, memory usage, allocation patterns, response latency and resource contention. Use profiling and runtime diagnostics to identify bottlenecks before changing configuration.\n\nPRODUCTION:\nIntegrate the design into CI/CD, secure configuration, monitoring, structured logging, health checks and documented rollback procedures. Review production metrics after deployment and validate recovery procedures.\n\nACCEPTANCE:\nThe implementation must compile, pass automated tests, preserve existing contracts, expose useful diagnostics and behave predictably under expected production failure conditions."
